<title>USA: US attache--meat market opportunities in Bulgaria.</title>
<headline>US attache--meat market opportunities in Bulgaria.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>An agricultural attache at the U.S. embassy in Sofia said U.S. exporters have a &quot;golden opportunity&quot; to expand sales of meat products to Bulgaria in the next few years due to low meat output there.</p>
<p>&quot;Marketing opportunities for U.S. meat exporters should open up dramatically for the remainder of the year and next year,&quot; the attache wrote in a report dated June 23 released in Washington on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the demand for imported pork will last only until domestic herds are rebuilt -- which may take years, the market for imported beef -- US$23 million in 1995 -- is indefinite as Bulgaria consistently has a shortage of good quality beef,&quot; the attache continued.</p>
<p>The attache said two other important factors which should increase demand for exports were that as of July 1 import duties for several meat products would be halved, and prices in general were liberalized this week.</p>
<p>Attache reports are not official USDA data.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
